# Jira commit linking

Every **task-related** commit must include a work-item key so Jira's **Development** panel (commits / branches / PRs) links correctly when GitHub is connected.

## Required subject format

```
<type>(<scope>)[<ISSUE-KEY>]: <imperative summary>
```

| Part | Rule |
|---|---|
| `<type>` | Conventional Commits: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf` |
| `<scope>` | Allowed scopes from `01-git-workflow.mdc` (`bookmarks`, `auth`, `billing`, `go`, …) |
| `[<ISSUE-KEY>]` | **Mandatory** on task commits — square brackets, uppercase `SB-N` |
| Summary | Imperative mood; whole subject ≤72 chars |

### Issue key precedence

1. **Jira leaf issue** — `[SB-N]` when the task exists on the board (orchestrator JIRA SYNC, user named `SB-*`, or roadmap row has a Jira mirror via `Roadmap ID` field)
2. **Roadmap only** — `[P2-01]` when no Jira issue exists yet
3. **Combined batch** — primary leaf key in brackets; list siblings in session memory

### Examples

```bash
# GOOD — Jira work
feat(auth)[SB-12]: add server-side session store with configurable TTL
fix(slugs)[SB-31]: resolve collision disambiguation when shared bookmark deleted

# GOOD — roadmap-only (no Jira mirror)
feat(workspaces)[P2-01]: implement workspace creation with entitlement check

# GOOD — plan-file verifier commit
chore(plan)[SB-12]: mark P1-03 verified

# BAD — key at end (old format)
feat(auth): add session store (SB-12)

# BAD — missing key on task work
feat(auth): add session store

# BAD — Smart Commit commands (MCP owns Jira sync)
feat(auth)[SB-12]: add session store #time 2h #comment done
```

## Smart Commits — NEVER use in commit messages

Jira sync (status, worklog, comments) is handled by **MCP** in orchestrated runs. Never put these in commit subjects or bodies:

- `#time`, `#comment`, `#resolve`, `#close`, or any `#<transition>` command

Issue keys alone link commits to work items; smart commands would duplicate worklogs and transition issues at the wrong time.

## Exceptions (no issue key required)

- Pure repo hygiene with no task ID: `chore(repo): init pnpm workspace` (rare; prefer an SB issue when in doubt)
- Integration merge commits: `chore(repo)[SB-N]: integrate orchestrator batch (<BATCH_ID>)`

## Enforcement

- **Execution agents:** implementation commits include `[SB-N]` or `[P*-*]`
- **Verifiers:** Layer 3 — FAIL if a task commit subject lacks a valid issue key when Jira sync was in scope
- **Orchestrator prompts:** pass leaf `SB-N` in the GIT block; see `.cursor/skills/orchestrator/prompt-templates.md`
